      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Key Cost Factors in Utah"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Home Size: Inspectors who charge by square footage typically charge $0.04 to $0.08 per square foot for residential properties. In mountain areas like Park City, complex architecture can push rates between $0.10 and $0.30 per square foot."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Pitch and Complexity: Steeper roofs require specialized safety gear or drones, which usually adds a $25 to $175 surcharge depending on the steepness."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Location: Labor rates and specialized winter-weather damage assessments (like checking for ice dam issues) can cause slight price variations between Salt Lake County, Northern Utah, and Southern Utah."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "To help narrow this down, please let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What is the approximate square footage or story count of the home?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What type of roof do you have (asphalt shingle, metal, tile)?"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "What is the purpose of the inspection (routine maintenance, buying/selling a home, or checking for storm damage)?"
